#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
TRBM-FLARE-VAX: Theory-Residual Behavioral Memory for NHIS influenza-vaccination prediction.

This driver preserves the exact deterministic V4/V5 HBM proxy construction from the
supplied FLARE-VAX code, but changes the prediction architecture so the frozen LLM is
NOT responsible for estimating the base vaccination probability.

Core design
-----------
1. Deterministic HBM layer
   Reuse the supplied V4/V5 feature-to-construct mappings and HBM8 patterns.

2. Theory-constrained numerical prior
   Fit a small logistic model using ONLY five positively oriented HBM-inspired
   constructs. Coefficients are constrained to be non-negative. V4 uses the
   prior-vaccine acceptance/benefit-consistent proxy; V5 replaces it with
   preventive engagement and excludes other-vaccine-history predictors.

3. Cross-fitted theory residuals
   On the memory split, produce out-of-fold probabilities and define
       residual_i = y_i - P_HBM_i.
   The LLM never creates this residual and never sees in-sample theory-prior
   predictions when residual memories are discovered.

4. LLM mechanism reflection
   Only high-magnitude memory residuals are sent to the frozen ASU LLM. The LLM
   explains which OBSERVED behavioral mechanism may account for the departure
   from the HBM prior. It does not output a probability or correction magnitude.

5. Theory-residual behavioral memory
   Each memory stores the OOF HBM prior, actual outcome, signed empirical residual,
   structured mechanism family/rule, and observable applicability evidence.

6. Test-time mechanism gating
   For a new respondent, retrieve theory-failure memories by HBM-state similarity
   plus contextual similarity. The LLM only decides whether a retrieved mechanism
   is applicable and in which direction. It still does not output a probability.

7. Empirical numerical correction
   Correction magnitude is computed from the signed historical residuals of the
   selected memories. A single global scale is calibrated on the calibration split,
   memory is then frozen, and the test split is evaluated once.

This is a theory-guided, training-free LLM adaptation layer. The LLM is never
fine-tuned. The HBM variables remain observed proxies rather than direct psychometric
measurements of all HBM beliefs.
"""

